# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PUBLISH BRANCH ("site"). This branch is pushed to a PUBLIC repo and served
# by GitHub Pages, so it carries the site and nothing else.
#
# The working tree is shared with the private branches, which means the files
# below are sitting on disk right next to the site while this branch is
# checked out. Without these rules a single `git add -A` publishes the career
# notes, the decision log and the internal audits. Keep them listed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Private working files — never published.
CLAUDE.md
MEMORY.md
MILESTONES.md
docs/
tools/
scratch/
node_modules/

# The dashboard is a LOCAL tool. It reads and writes data/projects.js on disk
# through the File System Access API; published, it would just be an internal
# control panel anyone can read. Run it locally with tools/devserve.py.
admin.html
admin.js
admin.css

# Source material and oversized media — see the private branch's .gitignore
# for the full reasoning. Repeated here because gitignore is per branch.
assets/pdf_projects/
assets/projects/house-walkthrough/house-walkthrough.mp4
assets/projects/opencv-grasshopper/comvis.gif
assets/projects/pcg-runtime/pcg-runtime-clip.mp4
